  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\r\n\r\nI would like to have a native attribute for the textarea that would increase or decrease the height of the textarea depending on the height of the textarea content.\r\n\r\n### What solutions exist today?\r\n\r\n#### html\r\n`<textarea oninput=\"auto_grow(this)\"></textarea>`\r\n\r\n#### JS\r\n```\r\nfunction auto_grow(element) {\r\n  element.style.height = \"5px\";\r\n  element.style.height = (element.scrollHeight) + \"px\";\r\n}\r\n```\r\n#### CSS\r\n```\r\ntextarea {\r\n  resize: none;\r\n  overflow: hidden;\r\n  min-height: 50px;\r\n  max-height: 100px;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### How would you solve it?\r\n\r\nYou can add a new attribute for textarea - auto-height or auto-rows. Another option is to expand the rows attribute by adding the value auto\r\n\r\n### Anything else?\r\n\r\n_No response_",
